{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6724895813","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901#issuecomment-6724895813","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/901","id":6724895813,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkNXERQ","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?u=4a54630ef210e4f76a452eea65cda1b56370734c&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T17:46:31Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T17:46:31Z","author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Current campaign review confirms a bounded remaining form-of predicate defect in `L-Cysteine_X_HCl_X_H2O_Solution.yaml`, related to the historical #342/#321 rationale tracked here.\n\nAt completed ancillary baseline84241993a278a7a413422ef89a52c0b47dc57831, authentic owner SHA256 is `ee8eca61baf20c28acd7bbf0409d44ea796fb33d988f6e81eb60b6fba67fc105`. The already reviewed worker07 alias-cleanup proposal `C-P04` has full payload `0ca4e6c9a4c7d05c99f64adffb1d4ab7c63cb31b618d2b3c74e26288831f16e2`; it still retains CLOSE_MATCH justified by absence of an is_a relation. Neither proposal nor correction has been applied in the corrected integration checkout.\n\n[JCM680](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=680) explicitly adds L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate solution,10mL. This is a receiving-medium addition volume, not a known stock concentration, solvent or pH. [CHEBI:91248](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:91248) denotes the monohydrate solute. Current MAPPING_SEMANTICS sections1/3 explicitly allow solution-to-solute broadMatch and forbid treating that as identity or subclass_of. The historical no-subclass rationale therefore does not support the current symmetric closeMatch.\n\nProposed bounded correction: retain local `kgmicrobe.ingredient:l-cysteine_x_hcl_x_h2o_solution`, STOCK_SOLUTION status, CHEBI:91248 parent, original histories and the reviewed unrelated-dye/instruction rejections. Change only the native grade CLOSE_MATCH to NARROW_MATCH, which emits `skos:broadMatch`, and append truthful claim-specific evidence/history with LLM assistance disclosed. Keep the exact local registry sibling. Do not transfer solute CAS/chemistry, invent concentration/composition, merge owners or approve roles/export claims.\n\nIndependent read-only assessment supports this route: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/inherited-form-predicate-independent-assessment-v1/HANDOFF.json`, SHA256 `624a8c931b210cd73ef9dc013b43aea43413e71421d2958ef761806a29aafa0a`. Actual JCM capture `16525b97d468855002dda4489f4b2030d28a9a1d332828cc27a0f2e15b5b07f0`; current full ChEBI capture `7ef9e26cec1a5833d216a01df066c0b6a0bfba77bad16db354c690a7a814a683`. Exact successor authoring, complete-byte independent re-review, guarded application, native generation and final validation remain required. This comment does not clear the wider cohort or its existing scientific holds.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6724895813/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}